<PARA INFOID = "T150004T079" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "25Apr2005"     INFOTYPE = "SYSTEM" INDSW = "ON" SELECT = "Customize">
<TITLE>Smart Entry &amp; Start Customization</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>There are 2 procedures for smart customization, as shown below. Set each function according to each operation procedure.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>

<MECA ID = "T150004T079T096" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "26May2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>List When Using Diagnostic Tool</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Connect the diagnostic tool "TaSCAN" to the DLC3 connector and select "Customize" → "Smart Entry &amp; Start" on the screen.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "4" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "22%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "22%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "3" COLNAME = "3" COLWIDTH = "44%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "4" COLNAME = "4" COLWIDTH = "9%"/>
<THEAD>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Diagnostic Tool Name</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Setting</PTXT>
<PTXT>(Initial settings are listed first)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Description</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "4" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Control ECU</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</THEAD>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Smart Ignition</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>All Seats<HINTREF REFID = "H285150004T079T09601"/>/Front (+ Rear1) Seats<HINTREF     REFID = "H285150004T079T09602"/></PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3" CONSPIC = "0"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM>
<PTXT>Setting of the engine start detection area for the Smart Entry &amp; Start System function</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "4" MOREROWS = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Certification ECU</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Standby Time in Parked State</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>2.5 s / 0.5 s / 1.5 s / 5 s</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3" CONSPIC = "0"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM>
<PTXT>Sets the time during which the doors do not unlock even if the door outside handle is operated after the doors are locked with the Smart Entry &amp; Start System function (door lock confirmation time)</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Smart Back Door</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Press and hold / ON 2 times / No function</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Setting of the back door unlock method for the Smart Entry &amp; Start System function</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP>
<LEGEND><HINT>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT ID = "H285150004T079T09601">Means possible at front seats, rear seats and back door</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT ID = "H285150004T079T09602">Means possible at front seats and rear seats</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></HINT></LEGEND></TABLE></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T150004T079T097" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "26May2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>List When Not Using Diagnostic Tool</TITLE>
<LIST1><TITLE>Key Cancel Function</TITLE>
<ITEM><PTXT>The Smart Entry &amp; Start System control below can be cancelled by performing certain operations.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1"><TITLE>Cancelable Items List</TITLE>
<TGROUP COLS = "1" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_00">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "99%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Smart Entry &amp; Start System Control</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Warning Function</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Function to Prevent Locking the Electronic Key in the Cabin</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>Smart Back Door Open Control</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>With the power OFF (ACC and IG OFF), driver door closed and driver door unlocked, the key cancel function can be set by performing the operations below.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1"><TITLE>Key Cancel Operation Procedure</TITLE>
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "9%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "90%"/>
<THEAD>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Procedure</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Operation</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</THEAD>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Prerequisites</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "LEFT"><PTXT>Driver door closed and unlocked, power OFF (IG and ACC OFF)</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Operation 1</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "LEFT"><PTXT>Perform wireless unlock 1 times</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Operation 2</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "LEFT"><PTXT>Open the driver door within 5 seconds of operation 1</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Operation 3</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "LEFT"><PTXT>Perform wireless unlock 2 times within 5 seconds of performing operation 2<HINTREF     REFID = "H285150004T079T09701"/></PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Operation 4</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "LEFT"><PTXT>Within 30 seconds of performing operation 3, repeat driver door "open" → "closed" 2 times and open it again (driver door "open" → "closed" → "open" → "closed" → "open")</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Operation 5</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "LEFT"><PTXT>Perform wireless unlock 2 times within 30 seconds of performing operation 4<HINTREF     REFID = "H285150004T079T09701"/></PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Operation 6</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "LEFT"><PTXT>Within 30 seconds of performing operation 5, repeat driver door open → closed 1 times and open it again (driver door "open" → "closed" → "open")</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>Operation 7</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE" ALIGN = "LEFT"><PTXT>Close the driver door within 5 seconds after performing operation 6<HINTREF     REFID = "H285150004T079T09702"/></PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
<HINT>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT ID = "H285150004T079T09701">If a driver door "open" → "closed" operation occurs during operations 3 and 5, the cancel function is aborted.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT ID = "H285150004T079T09702">To return from the key cancel state to a state in which the Smart Entry &amp; Start System can be used, perform the above "key cancel operation procedure" again.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></HINT>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1"><TITLE>Key Cancel Operation Answer-back</TITLE>
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "53%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "46%"/>
<THEAD>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Status</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Answer-back</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</THEAD>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>When Key Cancelled</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Wireless answer-back buzzer sounds 2 times</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>When Returning from Key Cancel State</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Wireless answer-back buzzer sounds 1 times</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></MECA>
</PARA>
<BIND ID = "T150004T079B" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Related Parts</TITLE>

<PARA INFOID = "T150003K791" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "21Apr2004"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>DLC3 (Data Link Connector No.3)</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>By connecting the diagnostic tool "TaSCAN" to the vehicle side connector (DLC3: Data Link Connector No.3), each ECU can be accessed via the gateway computer and the various multiplex communication lines. This allows output of DTCs, data monitoring (checking ECU data, etc.), Active Test (driving actuators as desired), customization (setting control programs), etc. For details, refer to the Repair Manual.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740048b" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "3.389in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</BIND>
</SECTION>